From: iafx <iafx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:51:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(valve): HD Haptics speaker taps on the Steam
 Controller's grips, over the cable

The Steam Controller (2026) has no speaker, but its grips play beeps and
chirps as well as a DualSense speaker does (iafx, by ear, on its cable). The
grip DSP now runs the HD Haptics speaker taps too: one generator per side,
each through the speaker high-pass and a 400 Hz high-pass (below that a grip
turns sound into vibration), and the packer adds them under the vibration
with a limiter that leaves anything up to the 0.8 ceiling unchanged. Only
format 8 (8 kHz, cable) carries them; at 4 kHz the band ends near 2 kHz.
The studio motor stays off on the grips. RENHDRUM_GRIP_SPEAKER_PERCENT
(0..100, 0 = off) sets the level, default HD_HAPTICS_SPEAKER_PERCENT (60).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
